   "source": [
    "# Module 1: R Fundamentals on ACS Child Welfare Data\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning path:** ACS Predictive Analytics Curriculum  \n",
    "**Dataset:** Simulated NYC ACS SCR Reports + Features  \n",
    "**Concepts covered:**\n",
    "- tidyverse: dplyr, tidyr, lubridate\n",
    "- ggplot2 visualization\n",
    "- Table joins across ACS tables\n",
    "- Missing data handling in R\n",
    "- R Shiny basics\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "**How to use this notebook:**  \n",
    "Run every cell. Read every comment. Try the exercises at the end of each section.  \n",
    "The goal is not to memorize syntax — it's to build intuition for what the data looks like.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SETUP — Install and load packages"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install packages (only need to do this once in Colab)\n",
    "# In Colab: Runtime > Change runtime type > R\n",
    "\n",
    "install.packages(c(\n",
    "  'tidyverse',   # dplyr + ggplot2 + tidyr + lubridate + more\n",
    "  'janitor',     # clean_names(), tabyl() - extremely useful\n",
    "  'skimr',       # skim() - better than summary()\n",
    "  'scales',      # number formatting in ggplot\n",
    "  'patchwork',   # combine multiple ggplot charts\n",
    "  'gt'           # beautiful tables\n",
    "), repos='https://cran.rstudio.com/', quiet=TRUE)\n",
    "\n",
    "library(tidyverse)\n",
    "library(janitor)\n",
    "library(skimr)\n",
    "library(scales)\n",
    "library(patchwork)\n",
    "library(gt)\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('All packages loaded successfully\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SECTION 1.1 — Load Data and First Look\n",
    "\n",
    "**Upload the two CSV files to Colab first:**  \n",
    "Left panel → Files icon → Upload → select acs_scr_reports.csv and acs_features.csv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load both tables\n",
    "scr      <- read_csv('acs_scr_reports.csv', show_col_types = FALSE)\n",
    "features <- read_csv('acs_features.csv',    show_col_types = FALSE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Always check shape first\n",
    "cat('SCR table:     ', nrow(scr),      'rows x', ncol(scr),      'columns\\n')\n",
    "cat('Features table:', nrow(features), 'rows x', ncol(features), 'columns\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# glimpse() is better than head() for understanding structure\n",
    "# Shows: column names, data types, first few values\n",
    "glimpse(scr)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# skim() gives a full data quality report in one call\n",
    "# Shows: missing counts, distributions, unique values\n",
    "# This is the FIRST thing you do with any new dataset\n",
    "skim(scr)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check missing data specifically in features table\n",
    "# THIS IS CRITICAL for ACS data - missingness is informative\n",
    "features %>%\n",
    "  summarise(across(everything(), ~ sum(is.na(.)))) %>%\n",
    "  pivot_longer(everything(), names_to = 'column', values_to = 'missing_count') %>%\n",
    "  mutate(\n",
    "    missing_pct  = round(missing_count / nrow(features) * 100, 1),\n",
    "    is_missing   = missing_count > 0\n",
    "  ) %>%\n",
    "  filter(is_missing) %>%\n",
    "  arrange(desc(missing_pct))\n",
    "\n",
    "# WHY THIS MATTERS:\n",
    "# days_since_last_report is missing when prior_reports_12mo == 0\n",
    "# That's STRUCTURAL missingness - not random\n",
    "# substance_use_flag missing = caseworker didn't document it\n",
    "# Both are informative signals, not noise"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# EXERCISE 1.1\n",
    "# Verify the structural missingness claim above:\n",
    "# When prior_reports_12mo == 0, days_since_last_report should ALWAYS be NA\n",
    "# When prior_reports_12mo > 0, days_since_last_report should NEVER be NA\n",
    "\n",
    "features %>%\n",
    "  mutate(has_prior = prior_reports_12mo > 0) %>%\n",
    "  group_by(has_prior) %>%\n",
    "  summarise(\n",
    "    n               = n(),\n",
    "    days_missing    = sum(is.na(days_since_last_report)),\n",
    "    days_present    = sum(!is.na(days_since_last_report)),\n",
    "    pct_missing     = round(days_missing / n * 100, 1)\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Expected: has_prior=FALSE -> 100% missing, has_prior=TRUE -> 0% missing\n",
    "# If that's what you see: missingness is structural, not random"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SECTION 1.2 — dplyr: The Core Verbs\n",
    "\n",
    "dplyr has 5 core verbs. Master these and you can do 90% of data manipulation.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Verb | What it does |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `filter()` | Keep rows matching a condition |\n",
    "| `select()` | Keep specific columns |\n",
    "| `mutate()` | Create or modify columns |\n",
    "| `group_by() + summarise()` | Aggregate by group |\n",
    "| `arrange()` | Sort rows |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# FILTER: Keep only Bronx cases\n",
    "bronx_cases <- scr %>%\n",
    "  filter(borough == 'Bronx')\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('Total cases:', nrow(scr), '\\n')\n",
    "cat('Bronx cases:', nrow(bronx_cases), '\\n')\n",
    "cat('Bronx share:', round(nrow(bronx_cases)/nrow(scr)*100, 1), '%\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# FILTER with multiple conditions\n",
    "# Physical abuse cases in Bronx with young children\n",
    "high_risk_bronx <- scr %>%\n",
    "  filter(\n",
    "    borough        == 'Bronx',\n",
    "    allegation_type == 'Physical Abuse',\n",
    "    child_age      <= 5\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('High risk Bronx cases (physical abuse, child <= 5):', nrow(high_risk_bronx), '\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "# DOMAIN INSIGHT: Physical abuse + young child is highest risk combination\n",
    "# Young children cannot advocate for themselves\n",
    "# This filter simulates what a caseworker triage would prioritize"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# SELECT: Choose specific columns\n",
    "scr %>%\n",
    "  select(report_id, family_id, borough, allegation_type, outcome) %>%\n",
    "  head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# MUTATE: Create new columns\n",
    "# Convert report_date to proper date type and extract useful components\n",
    "\n",
    "scr <- scr %>%\n",
    "  mutate(\n",
    "    report_date    = as.Date(report_date),\n",
    "    report_year    = year(report_date),\n",
    "    report_month   = month(report_date, label = TRUE),  # Jan, Feb, etc\n",
    "    report_quarter = quarter(report_date),\n",
    "    report_dow     = wday(report_date, label = TRUE),   # Mon, Tue, etc\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Severity classification - domain knowledge\n",
    "    allegation_severity = case_when(\n",
    "      allegation_type == 'Sexual Abuse'                          ~ 5,\n",
    "      allegation_type == 'Physical Abuse'                        ~ 4,\n",
    "      allegation_type == 'Domestic Violence Exposure'            ~ 3,\n",
    "      allegation_type %in% c('Neglect - Inadequate Supervision',\n",
    "                              'Neglect - Medical')               ~ 2,\n",
    "      TRUE                                                       ~ 1\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Was this case substantiated?\n",
    "    is_substantiated = outcome == 'Substantiated',\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Is this a mandated reporter?\n",
    "    is_mandated_reporter = reporter_type %in% c(\n",
    "      'School/Educational Staff', 'Hospital/Medical', 'Daycare/Childcare'\n",
    "    )\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check new columns\n",
    "scr %>%\n",
    "  select(report_date, report_year, report_month, report_quarter,\n",
    "         allegation_severity, is_substantiated, is_mandated_reporter) %>%\n",
    "  head(8)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# GROUP_BY + SUMMARISE: The most powerful combination\n",
    "# Reports by borough with substantiation rates\n",
    "\n",
    "borough_summary <- scr %>%\n",
    "  group_by(borough) %>%\n",
    "  summarise(\n",
    "    n_reports          = n(),\n",
    "    n_substantiated    = sum(is_substantiated, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
    "    substantiation_rate = round(mean(is_substantiated, na.rm = TRUE) * 100, 1),\n",
    "    avg_child_age      = round(mean(child_age), 1),\n",
    "    pct_physical_abuse = round(mean(allegation_type == 'Physical Abuse') * 100, 1),\n",
    "    avg_severity       = round(mean(allegation_severity), 2)\n",
    "  ) %>%\n",
    "  arrange(desc(n_reports))\n",
    "\n",
    "borough_summary\n",
    "\n",
    "# DOMAIN INSIGHT:\n",
    "# Higher substantiation rate = reporter types in that borough are more accurate\n",
    "# OR that borough has genuinely higher rates of maltreatment\n",
    "# You cannot distinguish these without further analysis\n",
    "# This is exactly the question ChildStat is trying to answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# GROUP_BY multiple variables\n",
    "# Reporter type breakdown by borough\n",
    "# This is ChildStat analysis — who is reporting from where?\n",
    "\n",
    "reporter_borough <- scr %>%\n",
    "  group_by(borough, reporter_type) %>%\n",
    "  summarise(\n",
    "    n_reports           = n(),\n",
    "    substantiation_rate = round(mean(is_substantiated, na.rm=TRUE)*100, 1),\n",
    "    .groups = 'drop'\n",
    "  ) %>%\n",
    "  arrange(borough, desc(n_reports))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show top 3 reporter types per borough\n",
    "reporter_borough %>%\n",
    "  group_by(borough) %>%\n",
    "  slice_max(n_reports, n = 3) %>%\n",
    "  print(n = 20)\n",
    "\n",
    "# KEY QUESTION: Is the top reporter type the same across boroughs?\n",
    "# Different boroughs may have different reporter composition\n",
    "# Bronx has more shelters -> shelter staff may report more\n",
    "# Manhattan has more hospitals -> medical reporters may dominate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# EXERCISE 1.2\n",
    "# Find the top 5 allegation types overall AND their substantiation rates\n",
    "# Then find which allegation type has the HIGHEST substantiation rate\n",
    "# What does that tell you about which reporters/situations lead to real findings?\n",
