    "\n",
    "allegation_summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SECTION 1.3 — Table Joins: Linking ACS Data Sources\n",
    "\n",
    "Real ACS work always involves linking multiple tables.  \n",
    "SCR table = intake. Features table = engineered risk variables.  \n",
    "You need both together to build the full picture per case.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Join type | What it keeps |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `left_join()` | All rows from left table, matching from right |\n",
    "| `inner_join()` | Only rows that match in BOTH tables |\n",
    "| `anti_join()` | Rows in left that have NO match in right |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# LEFT JOIN: Keep all SCR reports, attach features where available\n",
    "# This is the most common join for ACS work\n",
    "# You never want to lose a report just because features are missing\n",
    "\n",
    "full_data <- scr %>%\n",
    "  left_join(features, by = 'report_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('SCR rows:      ', nrow(scr), '\\n')\n",
    "cat('Full data rows:', nrow(full_data), '\\n')\n",
    "cat('Columns now:   ', ncol(full_data), '\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE: family_id appears in both tables\n",
    "# R automatically renames them family_id.x and family_id.y\n",
    "# Always check for duplicate columns after joining\n",
    "names(full_data)[str_detect(names(full_data), 'family')]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clean up duplicate columns after join\n",
    "full_data <- scr %>%\n",
    "  left_join(\n",
    "    features %>% select(-family_id),  # drop family_id from features before joining\n",
    "    by = 'report_id'\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('Clean join complete:', nrow(full_data), 'rows x', ncol(full_data), 'columns\\n')\n",
    "glimpse(full_data)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ANTI JOIN: Find SCR reports with NO features record\n",
    "# In real ACS work this would flag data quality issues\n",
    "\n",
    "missing_features <- scr %>%\n",
    "  anti_join(features, by = 'report_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('Reports missing from features table:', nrow(missing_features), '\\n')\n",
    "# In our simulated data this should be 0\n",
    "# In real ACS data this would be non-zero and worth investigating"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# FAMILY LEVEL AGGREGATION\n",
    "# Create one row per family summarizing their full history\n",
    "# This is how you'd build family-level features for the risk model\n",
    "\n",
    "family_history <- full_data %>%\n",
    "  arrange(family_id, report_date) %>%\n",
    "  group_by(family_id) %>%\n",
    "  summarise(\n",
    "    total_reports           = n(),\n",
    "    total_substantiated     = sum(is_substantiated, na.rm = TRUE),\n",
    "    substantiation_rate     = round(mean(is_substantiated, na.rm=TRUE)*100, 1),\n",
    "    first_report_date       = min(report_date),\n",
    "    last_report_date        = max(report_date),\n",
    "    days_in_system          = as.numeric(max(report_date) - min(report_date)),\n",
    "    n_distinct_reporters    = n_distinct(reporter_type),\n",
    "    n_distinct_allegations  = n_distinct(allegation_type),\n",
    "    max_severity            = max(allegation_severity),\n",
    "    boroughs_involved       = n_distinct(borough),\n",
    "    has_physical_abuse      = any(allegation_type == 'Physical Abuse'),\n",
    "    has_sexual_abuse        = any(allegation_type == 'Sexual Abuse'),\n",
    "    .groups = 'drop'\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('Unique families:', nrow(family_history), '\\n')\n",
    "family_history %>% arrange(desc(total_reports)) %>% head(10)\n",
    "\n",
    "# DOMAIN INSIGHT:\n",
    "# n_distinct_reporters is a powerful signal\n",
    "# A family reported by a school, a hospital, AND a neighbor independently\n",
    "# is much higher risk than a family reported 3x by the same school\n",
    "# Independent convergence of concern = stronger signal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# EXERCISE 1.3\n",
    "# Find all families with:\n",
    "#   - More than 3 reports\n",
    "#   - At least one substantiated outcome\n",
    "#   - Reports from 2+ different reporter types\n",
    "# These would be high-priority families for the risk model\n",
    "# How many such families exist in our dataset?\n",
    "\n",
    "high_priority_families <- family_history %>%\n",
    "  filter(\n",
    "    total_reports        > ___,\n",
    "    total_substantiated  >= ___,\n",
    "    n_distinct_reporters >= ___\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "cat('High priority families:', nrow(high_priority_families), '\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## SECTION 1.4 — ggplot2: Visualization for ACS Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "ggplot2 builds charts in layers:  \n",
    "`ggplot(data, aes(x, y))` → the canvas  \n",
    "`+ geom_*()` → the chart type  \n",
    "`+ labs()` → titles and labels  \n",
    "`+ theme_*()` → styling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# CHART 1: Reports by Borough (bar chart)\n",
    "# Most basic — how many reports per borough?\n",
    "\n",
    "p1 <- scr %>%\n",
    "  count(borough) %>%\n",
    "  mutate(borough = fct_reorder(borough, n)) %>%  # reorder by count\n",
    "  ggplot(aes(x = borough, y = n, fill = borough)) +\n",
    "  geom_col(show.legend = FALSE) +\n",
    "  geom_text(aes(label = n), hjust = -0.2, size = 4) +\n",
    "  coord_flip() +\n",
    "  scale_fill_brewer(palette = 'Blues', direction = -1) +\n",
    "  labs(\n",
    "    title    = 'SCR Reports by Borough',\n",
    "    subtitle = 'Bronx and Brooklyn account for majority of reports',\n",
    "    x        = NULL,\n",
    "    y        = 'Number of Reports',\n",
    "    caption  = 'Source: Simulated ACS SCR Data'\n",
    "  ) +\n",
    "  theme_minimal(base_size = 13) +\n",
    "  theme(plot.title = element_text(face = 'bold'))\n",
    "\n",
    "p1\n",
    "\n",
    "# WHY THIS CHART MATTERS FOR ACS:\n",
    "# Borough distribution is a fairness signal\n",
    "# If the risk model generates disproportionate false positives\n",
    "# in Bronx/Brooklyn, that's an equity problem\n",
    "# You need this baseline to interpret model fairness audit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# CHART 2: Monthly trend (time series)\n",
    "# Are reports increasing, decreasing, or seasonal?\n",
    "\n",
    "p2 <- scr %>%\n",
    "  mutate(year_month = floor_date(report_date, 'month')) %>%\n",
    "  count(year_month, borough) %>%\n",
    "  ggplot(aes(x = year_month, y = n, color = borough)) +\n",
    "  geom_line(linewidth = 0.8, alpha = 0.8) +\n",
    "  geom_smooth(method = 'loess', se = FALSE, linetype = 'dashed',\n",
    "              linewidth = 0.5, alpha = 0.5) +\n",
    "  scale_color_brewer(palette = 'Set1') +\n",
    "  scale_x_date(date_breaks = '6 months', date_labels = '%b %Y') +\n",
    "  labs(\n",
    "    title    = 'Monthly SCR Reports by Borough (2021-2024)',\n",
    "    subtitle = 'Dashed lines show smoothed trend',\n",
    "    x        = NULL,\n",
    "    y        = 'Reports per Month',\n",
    "    color    = 'Borough'\n",
    "  ) +\n",
    "  theme_minimal(base_size = 12) +\n",
    "  theme(\n",
    "    legend.position  = 'bottom',\n",
    "    plot.title       = element_text(face = 'bold'),\n",
    "    axis.text.x      = element_text(angle = 45, hjust = 1)\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "p2\n",
    "\n",
    "# DOMAIN INSIGHT:\n",
    "# Seasonality in child welfare reporting is real\n",
    "# School year = more educational neglect reports (mandated reporters active)\n",
    "# Summer = drop in school reports, increase in neighbor/community reports\n",
    "# ChildStat monitors this monthly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# CHART 3: Allegation type heatmap by borough\n",
    "# Which allegations are most common in each borough?\n",
    "\n",
    "p3 <- scr %>%\n",
    "  count(borough, allegation_type) %>%\n",
    "  group_by(borough) %>%\n",
    "  mutate(pct = n / sum(n) * 100) %>%\n",
    "  ungroup() %>%\n",
    "  mutate(\n",
    "    allegation_type = str_wrap(allegation_type, width = 20),\n",
    "    borough = fct_reorder(borough, -n, sum)\n",
    "  ) %>%\n",
    "  ggplot(aes(x = borough, y = allegation_type, fill = pct)) +\n",
    "  geom_tile(color = 'white', linewidth = 0.5) +\n",
    "  geom_text(aes(label = paste0(round(pct,1),'%')), size = 3.2) +\n",
    "  scale_fill_gradient(low = '#EFF3FF', high = '#2171B5',\n",
    "                      name = '% of\\nBorough Reports') +\n",
    "  labs(\n",
    "    title    = 'Allegation Type Distribution by Borough',\n",
    "    subtitle = 'Color intensity = % share within each borough',\n",
    "    x        = NULL,\n",
    "    y        = NULL\n",
    "  ) +\n",
    "  theme_minimal(base_size = 11) +\n",
    "  theme(\n",
    "    plot.title      = element_text(face = 'bold'),\n",
    "    axis.text.x     = element_text(angle = 30, hjust = 1),\n",
    "    legend.position = 'right'\n",
    "  )\n",
    "\n",
    "p3\n",
    "\n",
